    {
      "id": "clm_01M4VCA0BQ2R57MWAW2HQTSF97",
      "statement": "Josiah died in 609 BC, during Necho's march north and before the Egyptian crossing of the Euphrates in Du'ûzu.",
      "layer": "reconstruction",
      "passage": "2Kgs.23.29",
      "classification": "historically_plausible",
      "reasoning": "Kings places the death during Necho's march to the Euphrates; ABC 3 dates that campaign's crossing to Du'ûzu 609; the three months of Jehoahaz and the installation of Jehoiakim follow (2 Kgs 23:31–34), consistent with Jehoiakim's fourth year = 605 (Jer 46:2; ABC 5). The chronicle does not name Josiah. Classified historically plausible rather than strongly supported because only one independent line (ABC 3) supports the year directly.",
      "supporting_evidence": [
        "evd_01M4VCA0BQT7KMN899M41EQT0E"
      ],
      "counterevidence": [],
      "contextual_evidence": [
