      "id": "clm_01M4VCA0BQSQCMRCTNXD9Y1FRP",
      "statement": "Josiah died at Megiddo (2 Kgs 23:29) rather than after being brought back to Jerusalem.",
      "layer": "reconstruction",
      "passage": "2Kgs.23.29-2Kgs.23.30",
      "classification": "disputed",
      "reasoning": "Kings: Necho \"killed him at Megiddo\" and his servants \"carried him dead\". 2 Chr 35:23–24: wounded by archers, moved to a second chariot, brought to Jerusalem, \"and he died\". Josephus: he retreated to Jerusalem and \"died of that wound\". Keil holds that Chronicles does not say where he died; Lumby reports a view, from Zech 12:11, that he died at Hadad-rimmon. No external source bears on it.",
