      "id": "clm_01M4VCA0BSGEC4TRM7BXTQQF63",
      "statement": "Herodotus's battle at \"Magdolos\" against \"the Syrians\" (2.159) is Necho's battle at Megiddo.",
      "layer": "reconstruction",
      "passage": null,
      "classification": "historically_plausible",
      "reasoning": "Herodotus places a land victory of Necho at Magdolos followed by the capture of Cadytis. Keil explains Magdolos as a confusion with Megiddo; Movers (via Keil) placed it at Migdol on the Egyptian frontier. Herodotus is a fifth-century Greek source dependent on Egyptian informants.",
